WEBVTT

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:06.060
Leave this out...

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:08.880
Put one of these in...

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:12.840
Is it more balanced this way?

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:13.270
No, wait...

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:15.320
Gotta think this through...

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:25.450
Kamui, if you try too hard, you'll be worn 
out by the actual final round tomorrow.

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:28.420
Mmm, just a little more...

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:33.120
I guess this card would be better 
than that one, after all...

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:37.200
Go home and get some sleep!

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:39.300
R-Right!

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:42.410
We're leaving tomorrow morning at 7:00!

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:44.180
Gotcha!

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:46.280
Yeesh...

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:49.620
There is a lot to think about.

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:27.990
Our next topic is the final round of 
the Vanguard National Championship,

00:02:27.990 --> 00:02:29.480
which takes place tomorrow.

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:33.740
The two teams participating are Team AL4,

00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:36.760
going for their third win 
in a row, and Team Q4...

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:39.100
Dr. O, what do you predict?

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:43.930
Of course, AL4, which has been undefeated 
up to the last round, is likely to win.

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:47.040
They're not known as the 
strongest team for nothing.

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:52.560
What's the secret behind 
AL4's amazing strength?

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:56.790
Frankly, the team owes all of its victories

00:02:56.790 --> 00:03:00.970
to the intense conviction of its 
leader, Ren Suzugam-<i>oh</i>-ri!

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:03.860
I see. Thank you very much.

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:12.900
Fighting for the Top Spot

00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:19.540
Boy, that Aichi...

00:03:20.110 --> 00:03:22.830
What's he been doing all this time?

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:26.660
He did say he'd be a little 
late before he went out...

00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:28.100
Huh...

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:30.430
I'm home!

00:03:34.970 --> 00:03:36.290
Welcome back.

00:03:36.630 --> 00:03:39.560
Hey, I was worried about you!

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:41.380
Th-Thank you.

00:03:41.380 --> 00:03:42.390
Sorry.

00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:46.280
What about dinner?

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:51.090
Sorry. I'm not very... hungry...

00:03:52.060 --> 00:03:53.650
I'll eat later.

00:03:54.570 --> 00:03:59.060
It's wrapped, so when you do get 
hungry, just pop it in the microwave.

00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:00.530
Thank you.

00:04:02.810 --> 00:04:03.990
Aichi...?

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:07.300
Let's leave him alone for a while.

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:08.000
Okay.

00:04:17.270 --> 00:04:18.890
No trigger, huh?

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:31.530
I win.

00:04:33.820 --> 00:04:36.680
I never thought that Kai would lose...

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:40.880
Tomorrow, it'll be my turn to fight Ren.

00:04:41.590 --> 00:04:45.550
Can I possibly win against the person 
that even Kai was no match for?

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:53.140
Even so, I have to fight.

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:58.160
I'm...

00:05:02.840 --> 00:05:06.610
...putting everything on the 
line tomorrow to fight Ren.

00:05:42.370 --> 00:05:43.820
I can see you, Aichi...

00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:47.500
I can see you helpless before my power,

00:05:47.500 --> 00:05:48.770
suffering defeat...

00:06:03.290 --> 00:06:05.010
Misaki!

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:09.010
Do you remember where I put the 
tournament administrative documents?

00:06:09.010 --> 00:06:10.640
In the trunk.

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:12.260
Oh, that's right...

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:15.690
Oh, where's the car key?! Car key!

00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:16.420
Huh?

00:06:16.420 --> 00:06:17.820
In your right pocket.

00:06:18.650 --> 00:06:19.890
Oh, yes, that's right!

00:06:19.890 --> 00:06:21.550
Um, what else...?

00:06:21.950 --> 00:06:23.260
He's too high-strung.

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:25.760
Misaki!

00:06:26.350 --> 00:06:27.880
Good morning!

00:06:27.880 --> 00:06:28.870
Morning.

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:31.760
Good morning, Misaki.

00:06:32.230 --> 00:06:34.480
Have you come to see him off, Emi?

00:06:34.740 --> 00:06:37.600
After all, I'd worry about 
letting Aichi go alone.

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:41.000
Kamui isn't here yet...

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:43.270
Is everybody ready?

00:06:43.790 --> 00:06:44.270
Um...

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:46.970
Hey! Wait for me!

00:06:47.730 --> 00:06:49.620
I'm late! I'm late!

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:51.630
IT!

00:06:51.630 --> 00:06:53.270
In time!

00:06:53.270 --> 00:06:55.570
Just made it!

00:06:56.530 --> 00:06:59.280
Morning, Kamui. Are you okay?

00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:01.250
Y-Yeah...

00:07:01.490 --> 00:07:04.540
This is why I told you to 
go home and get some sleep!

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:06.990
Kamui, did you get up late?

00:07:06.990 --> 00:07:08.800
M-Miss Emi!

00:07:09.760 --> 00:07:11.260
Gyood myorning!

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:12.740
He can't even say that!

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:14.430
CES!

00:07:15.010 --> 00:07:18.500
No, I didn't oversleep. See... uh...

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:23.970
I-I kept going over my deck, and before I 
knew it, it was the middle of the night...

00:07:23.970 --> 00:07:26.040
So you got up late!

00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:27.730
GUL, yo!

00:07:27.730 --> 00:07:28.740
Yeah, I did...

00:07:30.150 --> 00:07:32.530
Well, we're about ready to go.

00:07:33.570 --> 00:07:34.750
Where's Kai?

00:07:36.400 --> 00:07:38.980
I don't think Kai's coming.

00:07:40.260 --> 00:07:41.360
He's not coming?

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:42.670
Right.

00:07:43.140 --> 00:07:46.190
I see... Okay, then.

00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:49.220
In that case, it'll just 
be you three fighting.

00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:51.130
So let's go!

00:07:51.430 --> 00:07:52.470
Okay.

00:07:52.470 --> 00:07:53.330
Yeah.

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:58.670
Jeez, what a jerk! How could Kai do 
this to us on such an important day?!

00:07:58.670 --> 00:07:59.760
Kamui...

00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:01.860
Yes, Miss Emi?!

00:08:02.200 --> 00:08:06.050
Aichi's been kind of down since yesterday...

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:12.620
I'm worried about him.

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:15.490
It'll be all right, Miss Emi!

00:08:16.360 --> 00:08:18.710
Leave your brother to me!

00:08:19.130 --> 00:08:21.770
You can rest queasy, knowing 
he's in good tails!

00:08:21.770 --> 00:08:23.620
Kamui the Great... That's "rest <i>easy</i>".

00:08:23.620 --> 00:08:25.920
It's because he's too nervous, TN, yo!

00:08:27.760 --> 00:08:29.320
Thank you!

00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:31.460
I'll get there by train so 
I can cheer you guys on.

00:08:31.800 --> 00:08:34.070
Great! Thank you!

00:08:34.070 --> 00:08:35.990
I promise you I'll win!

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:39.140
You guys, F-court Miss Emi there!

00:08:39.140 --> 00:08:41.410
Close! I think you meant "escort"...

00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:42.710
OK, yo!

00:08:43.140 --> 00:08:44.410
See you later!

00:08:58.290 --> 00:09:01.920
I-It's gonna be okay! I'll do my best!

00:09:03.170 --> 00:09:04.210
Um...

00:09:04.510 --> 00:09:06.970
Right. Let's all three do our best!

00:09:11.140 --> 00:09:15.230
I caused trouble for the team at 
the last national tournament...

00:09:15.230 --> 00:09:17.860
I have to make up for that, 
so please count on me!

00:09:19.150 --> 00:09:22.820
Kamui, no one here cares 
about what happened last...

00:09:22.820 --> 00:09:24.880
I haven't forgiven <i>myself</i>!

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:26.850
That's why today, I...

00:09:27.680 --> 00:09:30.220
That's why he's so eager...

00:09:30.220 --> 00:09:31.820
It's the final round.

00:09:32.150 --> 00:09:37.290
All the scores you guys want to settle, 
take them with you to the fight...

00:09:49.320 --> 00:09:50.350
Yeah...

00:10:15.960 --> 00:10:19.990
When it comes to the final round of the 
national tournament, I get all nervous!

00:10:21.200 --> 00:10:25.450
It's not like <i>we're</i> fighting. Let's 
just take it easy and cheer them on!

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:27.840
You've got a point...

00:10:27.840 --> 00:10:31.100
Even though we got here really early, 
look at all these people...

00:10:31.100 --> 00:10:33.610
So, where did Lose-umi go?

00:10:33.610 --> 00:10:35.460
Um, Morikawa is...

00:10:35.460 --> 00:10:38.670
Never mind. I've got a pretty good idea...

00:10:38.670 --> 00:10:39.980
I bought 'em!

00:10:40.150 --> 00:10:48.830
Love

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:43.400
Look at all the loot I got!

00:10:43.400 --> 00:10:48.860
All this Kourin merchandise is only 
being sold today, at the final match!

00:10:48.860 --> 00:10:51.790
They were sold out five 
minutes after opening!

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:54.520
But I was lined up from the start, 
so the early bird gets the worms!

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:57.040
Okay, okay. Good for you.

00:10:57.040 --> 00:10:58.490
I figured as much...

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:01.700
My national tournament...

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:03.540
...is over.

00:11:03.540 --> 00:11:04.730
It's not over for us!

00:11:05.430 --> 00:11:09.740
Jeez! The most important part 
hasn't even started yet!

00:11:13.700 --> 00:11:15.430
Yikes! Just five more minutes!

00:11:20.820 --> 00:11:22.810
Ouch!

00:11:22.810 --> 00:11:25.050
Hey, watch where you're going!

00:11:27.710 --> 00:11:30.990
Tetsu Shinjou from Team AL4!

00:11:46.290 --> 00:11:49.180
Tetsu Shinjou from Team AL4!

00:11:53.420 --> 00:11:54.890
Are you okay, boy?

00:12:00.580 --> 00:12:02.540
Spectator seating is over that way.

00:12:04.720 --> 00:12:08.430
Tetsu, what are you doing? It's almost time.

00:12:08.430 --> 00:12:10.180
A kid got lost...

00:12:11.910 --> 00:12:13.690
Spectator seating?

00:12:13.690 --> 00:12:15.150
Lost kid?!

00:12:15.560 --> 00:12:19.440
Idiot! I'm a participant!

00:12:24.590 --> 00:12:26.510
Hey, there she is.

00:12:26.510 --> 00:12:29.100
Miwa, Izaki, Lose-umi!

00:12:31.470 --> 00:12:34.450
Hello! It's good to see you again today.

00:12:36.450 --> 00:12:39.080
Um... Yeah, me too.

00:12:41.910 --> 00:12:46.250
Well, here we are. The final round 
of the Vanguard Championship.

00:12:46.250 --> 00:12:48.550
It's a full house here at the 
stadium, with every spectator

00:12:48.550 --> 00:12:53.050
eagerly awaiting the appearance of the 
teams that will engage in the final battle!

00:12:53.050 --> 00:12:55.110
It's s-<i>o</i> exciting!

00:13:20.610 --> 00:13:23.340
I'm trickling with enticement!

00:13:23.610 --> 00:13:25.310
That's trembling with excitement.

00:13:26.420 --> 00:13:29.970
Nice malaprop to ease the 
tension there, Kamui.

00:13:29.970 --> 00:13:30.560
Huh?

00:13:31.860 --> 00:13:35.790
Well, let's make this Team Q4's finest day!

00:13:36.060 --> 00:13:36.820
Right.

00:13:37.810 --> 00:13:38.670
Yeah!

00:13:39.610 --> 00:13:40.380
Okay!

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:51.010
And now, the curtain opens on the final round

00:13:51.010 --> 00:13:53.150
of the Vanguard National Championship!

00:14:00.620 --> 00:14:04.070
The strongest team in the country, AL4, 
going for their third win in a row

00:14:04.070 --> 00:14:08.530
versus a promising team that's making 
their second appearance here, Team Q4!

00:14:10.880 --> 00:14:14.340
I'll announce the pairings 
of this remarkable fight.

00:14:14.400 --> 00:14:16.150
Final Round
Team FFAL4 VS Team Q4

00:14:15.060 --> 00:14:19.350
The first match pits 
Tetsu Shinjou of Team AL4

00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:23.080
against Kamui Katsuragi of Team Q4!

00:14:23.710 --> 00:14:24.870
You...

00:14:26.120 --> 00:14:30.750
I have a feeling this is g-<i>o</i>-ing to be 
a fight with a lot of sights to see!

00:14:30.750 --> 00:14:33.310
<i>Oh</i>, indeed it is! I can't wait!

00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:36.080
All right, moving on to the next match-up...

00:14:36.630 --> 00:14:41.840
The second match will have Asaka 
Narumi versus Misaki Tokura!

00:14:42.320 --> 00:14:44.280
<i>Oh!</i> That'll be

00:14:44.280 --> 00:14:48.900
a revenge match for T-<i>o</i>-kura of Team Q4!

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:50.860
I'm s-<i>o</i> excited!

00:14:50.860 --> 00:14:52.790
And for the showcase, the final match...

00:14:53.080 --> 00:14:56.590
It'll be Ren Suzugamori versus Aichi Sendou!

00:14:58.750 --> 00:15:00.080
Hello.

00:15:06.070 --> 00:15:07.980
It's here at last!

00:15:07.980 --> 00:15:14.990
The final round of the Vanguard National 
Championship is about to begin!

00:15:11.330 --> 00:15:13.040
Tetsu Shinjou     Kamui Katsuragi

00:15:13.040 --> 00:15:14.540
Asaka Narumi     Misaki Tokura

00:15:14.540 --> 00:15:16.330
Ren Suzugamori     Aichi Sendou

00:15:19.740 --> 00:15:20.990
Are you anxious?

00:15:21.800 --> 00:15:25.930
Of course! This will decide who 
the strongest Cardfighter is!

00:15:27.580 --> 00:15:29.880
It'd be nice if that boy won, huh?

00:15:29.880 --> 00:15:31.720
Shall I cheer him on for you?

00:15:32.100 --> 00:15:33.490
Do what you want.

00:15:33.710 --> 00:15:38.470
Hey, Suiko, who do you hope will 
win, the boy or Ren Suzugamori?

00:15:39.140 --> 00:15:40.830
I don't have a preference.

00:15:41.300 --> 00:15:42.270
I told you before.

00:15:42.600 --> 00:15:45.620
Everything depends on the 
guidance of the cards.

00:15:46.250 --> 00:15:47.740
The first match...

00:15:48.110 --> 00:15:52.490
And here comes the strongest 
General, Tetsu Shinjou.

00:15:52.490 --> 00:15:54.490
S-<i>o</i> exciting, isn't it?!

00:15:54.920 --> 00:15:58.260
And his opponent, Team Q4's Kamui Katsuragi,

00:15:58.260 --> 00:16:01.530
making his first appearance 
at the national championship!

00:16:01.530 --> 00:16:04.730
What kind of fight are they going to show us?

00:16:05.620 --> 00:16:07.940
It's Kamui's first appearance?

00:16:07.940 --> 00:16:13.410
Remember how he had a fight with Kai last 
time around and ran out on the team?

00:16:14.180 --> 00:16:15.660
Now that you mention it...

00:16:16.640 --> 00:16:20.240
Oh, come on! An adult's fighting a kid?

00:16:20.240 --> 00:16:22.200
That's what it looks like!

00:16:22.200 --> 00:16:26.540
His first time here and his opponent's 
the General? What an unlucky guy!

00:16:26.540 --> 00:16:27.730
For real!

00:16:33.050 --> 00:16:37.850
It sounds like the people think 
<i>I</i> should be out there instead!

00:16:37.850 --> 00:16:39.650
Y-You think so?!

00:16:40.090 --> 00:16:43.740
Cut it out, Lose-umi! Just you 
being here is enough of a joke!

00:16:43.740 --> 00:16:45.750
EJ, yo!

00:16:45.750 --> 00:16:47.160
It's Katsumi!

00:16:48.080 --> 00:16:52.930
Morikawa, pay attention! Not just your 
name; he dissed your entire existence.

00:16:53.420 --> 00:16:56.720
Kamui the Great... Kamui the Great...

00:16:56.720 --> 00:16:59.940
...intends to make up for causing the 
team problems at that last tournament

00:17:00.290 --> 00:17:03.190
by doing his best here in the final round!

00:17:03.190 --> 00:17:06.710
SFU! He's seriously fired up!

00:17:06.710 --> 00:17:08.780
So don't make fun of him!

00:17:10.250 --> 00:17:14.130
A-All right, all right! 
I'm gonna cheer him on!

00:17:25.300 --> 00:17:26.450
Kamui...

00:17:30.410 --> 00:17:34.430
This is a surprise, you being my opponent, boy...

00:17:35.690 --> 00:17:39.240
I'm Kamui Katsuragi of Team Q4!

00:17:40.130 --> 00:17:44.330
I'll decide whether you're a fighter 
worthy of being called by name.

00:17:44.760 --> 00:17:46.020
What?!

00:17:46.430 --> 00:17:48.900
All right, so, the final round 
of the national championship...

00:17:48.900 --> 00:17:50.430
Let's begin!

00:17:50.430 --> 00:17:52.770
Let's start!

00:17:53.390 --> 00:17:55.240
Let the match begin!

00:18:06.630 --> 00:18:09.050
Stand up, Vanguard!

00:18:24.500 --> 00:18:25.860
I go first...

00:18:26.550 --> 00:18:27.150
Draw!

00:18:28.210 --> 00:18:31.210
Kamui the Great rides... Blaupanzer!

00:18:35.850 --> 00:18:37.770
Blaujunger's skill!

00:18:37.770 --> 00:18:41.640
When you ride Panzer, you get to 
add one Blaukluger to your hand!

00:18:41.960 --> 00:18:45.380
Also, Blaupanzer gains +2000 power!

00:18:47.700 --> 00:18:48.910
That's the end of my turn.

00:18:50.820 --> 00:18:51.600
Here I go.

00:18:55.580 --> 00:18:58.130
I ride... Prisoner Beast!

00:19:01.700 --> 00:19:03.850
Vermillion Gatekeeper's skill.

00:19:04.230 --> 00:19:05.440
Soulcharge!

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:08.020
Prisoner Beast attacks!

00:19:08.730 --> 00:19:09.830
No guard!

00:19:12.070 --> 00:19:13.500
Drive check!

00:19:18.060 --> 00:19:19.410
Damage check!

00:19:20.830 --> 00:19:22.170
My turn's over.

00:19:27.310 --> 00:19:29.820
So Kai didn't come...?

00:19:30.450 --> 00:19:32.590
I stand and draw!

00:19:33.770 --> 00:19:35.260
Blaukluger...

00:19:39.360 --> 00:19:42.830
He's not even lookin' at me!

00:19:42.830 --> 00:19:44.410
Insult me, will he?!

00:19:44.850 --> 00:19:46.790
Hey! Look over here!

00:19:47.930 --> 00:19:51.150
Kamui the Great rides Blaukluger!

00:19:56.190 --> 00:19:59.840
Blaupanzer is in the Soul, so 
Blaukluger gets +1000 power!

00:20:01.470 --> 00:20:06.370
I call Screamin' and Dancin' 
Announcer, Shout and Street Bouncer!

00:20:12.490 --> 00:20:14.760
I activate Street Bouncer's skill!

00:20:15.160 --> 00:20:18.490
I rest these two units and draw one card!

00:20:19.910 --> 00:20:22.280
I call Death Army Lady and Death Army Guy!

00:20:28.120 --> 00:20:29.690
With a boost from Death Army Guy,

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:32.310
Death Army Lady attacks!

00:20:39.790 --> 00:20:41.900
Blaukluger attacks!

00:20:43.160 --> 00:20:44.280
No guard.

00:20:44.740 --> 00:20:46.000
Drive check!

00:20:50.710 --> 00:20:51.730
Check.

00:20:55.150 --> 00:20:57.760
Yes! He took 2 damage!

00:20:57.760 --> 00:20:59.390
That's unusual...

00:20:59.390 --> 00:20:59.890
Yeah...

00:21:00.370 --> 00:21:05.410
Normally, his play style is to launch a 
swift attack, even with only grade 0 cards.

00:21:07.500 --> 00:21:11.100
I can't afford to carelessly 
lay out grade 0 units...

00:21:11.100 --> 00:21:12.420
Not against his deck...

00:21:26.380 --> 00:21:30.350
W-With this, what happens 
to Soul Saver Dragon?

00:21:30.650 --> 00:21:33.300
This is the skill of Stil Vampir.

00:21:33.870 --> 00:21:39.430
During this turn, my enemy's Vanguard 
becomes the rear-guard of my choosing...

